# Wrangler's local cache. Holds the Cloudflare account id and account name. Neither is a
# credential, but neither belongs in a public repo. worker/.gitignore has covered the copy
# under worker/ since the first time this happened; running wrangler from the repo root
# creates a second one HERE, which that rule never saw. Ignore it wherever it lands.
.wrangler/
